-- title:
--   Supersingular k₀-level valuation ring and smooth-point stalks, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $\kappa$ the residue field of a valuation subring $A\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $F=$ `fieldBar q M'` the field obtained from the level-$H$ modular function field of level $q^2M'$ (with $H=$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$) by base change of coefficients to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ inside Laurent series, and `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` the corresponding base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` $\subset$ `LaurentSeries ℚ`.
--
--   *Level and residue data.* Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell_0$ be a prime with $\ell_0\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_0\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\kappa$ which, by the hypothesis `hW`, consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational (the map $\kappa\to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ on the geometric $j$-generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q κ`. A place $s\in W$ is fixed.
--
--   *Reduction data.* The hypothesis `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ $F$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the base-changed level-$M'$ field together with a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the characteristic-$p$ modular function field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places preserving degrees, compatibility of membership and of residues with $A$, the scaling property that every nonzero $f$ admits $c$ with $c\cdot f$ integral of nonzero residue, and the compatibility of divisors with $\mathrm{placeMap}$. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies this reduction with coefficientwise reduction of $q$-expansions: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Small constants.* Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ with $\pi_0\in A$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require that $A\cap k_0$ (formally, the comap of $A$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$) be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, and with algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` requires that every $a\in A$ be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary prime and constants.* Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; let $\zeta_0\in k_0$ be a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and let $\varpi_t\in k_0$ satisfy $\varpi_t\in A$ and $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *Layers.* Let $\iota$ be a type, $K:\iota\to$ intermediate fields of $k_0\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with each $K_n$ finite over $k_0$, and $A_n$ a valuation subring of $K_n$ with $x\in A_n\iff x\in A$ for all $x\in K_n$.
--
--   The conclusion, with $k_0$ acting on $F$ through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, asserts the existence of an intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subset F$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the following hold.
--
--   (i) $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $F_0$ generate $F$: the join of `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ↥(fieldBar q M')))` with $F_0$ is $\top$.
--
--   (ii) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (iii) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (iv) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (v) There is $t\in W_0$ with the following property: for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)\in W_0$ and $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then every coefficient of $p$ has image in $W_0$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (vi) For every $g\in$ `LaurentSeries ℚ` lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, whose image under coefficientwise embedding into `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, and which satisfies: at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the $q$-expansion $j_q$ has non-negative order, $g$ has non-negative order; and the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ — the image of $g$ in $F$ under the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$ there, and for every $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference between the image of $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (vii) For every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ maps $F_0$ into itself, and for $f\in F_0$ whose image also lies in $F_0$, $f\in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (viii) For every field $FSS$ with an algebra structure over $\kappa$ and every `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ on $F$ with values in $FSS$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ with surjective residue map onto $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, and with the scaling property), if $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}\iff f\in W_0$ for all $f\in F_0$, then both of the following hold.
--
--   (viii-a) For every algebra structure of $\mathbb F_{q^2}=$ `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e:FSS\xrightarrow{\sim}$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements of $C_s$) such that $\#C_s=2\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s` (the quotient of `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of $s$ by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; for $q=3$ the numerator is $6$ at $j=0$ and $1$ otherwise), and such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ for which `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and for which $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the automorphism of $FSS$ induced by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` corresponds under $e$, inside the Drinfeld function field, to the action `hFunctionFieldAction` of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$.
--
--   (viii-b) There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$, subrings $S_{Q,n}\subset F$, ring maps $\varphi_{Q,n}:A_n[X]\to S_{Q,n}$ and $\chi_{Q,n}:S_{Q,n}\to\kappa$, and sets $D_{Q,n}$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with $\#N=q+1$, such that for every place $Q\notin N$ the following hold.
--
--   For every layer $n$: the residue map $A_n\to\kappa$ is surjective; the images of $A_n$ lie in $S_{Q,n}$; $\varphi_{Q,n}$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in $F$ and $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(X))=0$; for every $c\in A_n$ with residue $0$ there is a unique ring map $\chi:S_{Q,n}\to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a))=a$ for all $a$, with residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X))=c$; every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and its residue there is the image of $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has order $1$ at $Q$; a place $P$ belongs to $D_{Q,n}$ exactly when $P$ is rational, every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and for every $f$ one has $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ if and only if $\chi_{Q,n}(f)=0$; $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)\ne\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,c)$ for every $c\in A_n$; $S_{Q,n}$ is local with maximal ideal the zero set of $\chi_{Q,n}$, Noetherian, and a unique factorisation monoid; $S_{Q,n}$ is contained in the join $E_n$ of `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀` of the image of $K_n$ with $F_0$, and every element of $E_n$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in S_{Q,n}$, $h\ne 0$; the elements of $E_n$ are $K_n$-linearly disjoint from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the sense that for every finite family $c_i\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K_n$ and every family $a_i\in E_n$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ one has all $a_i=0$; every ring map $\chi:S_{Q,n}\to A_n$ satisfying the two compatibilities above has kernel generated by $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)-\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)))$; there is a nonzero generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$ such that $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ is prime, such that for $f\in E_n$ one has $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in S_{Q,n}$ and $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)\nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_{Q,n}$ not associated to $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x\in S_{Q,n}$ there is a monic polynomial $r$ over $A_n$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of the image of $r$ under $\varphi_{Q,n}\circ C$; and there is a finite subset $G\subset S_{Q,n}$ such that every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ can be written as $g/h$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, $h$ being a unit of $S_{Q,n}$.
--
--   Moreover the charts are compatible across layers: $K_n\le K_{n'}$ implies $S_{Q,n}\subseteq S_{Q,n'}$ and $S_{Q,n'}$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_{Q,n}$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$; the element $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ is the same for all $n$; and $\chi_{Q,n'}$ restricted along the inclusion agrees with $\chi_{Q,n}$.
--
--   Finally: for $Q,Q'\notin N$, if some place $P$ lies in both $D_{Q,n}$ and $D_{Q',n}$ for some $n$, then $Q=Q'$; for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_{Q,n}$, the image of $j_q$ in $F$ has non-negative order at $P$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ that preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every place $Q$ of $FSS$, one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q\in N$ if and only if $Q\in N$, and if $Q\notin N$ then `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)` $=D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q,\,n}$ for every $n$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ instance of the construction, over the field of small constants $k_0$, of a discrete valuation ring $W_0$ on the level-$q^2M'$ modular function field which specialises the chosen supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ curve, together with the Drinfeld-curve description of the resulting special fibre and with smooth-point charts $(S_{Q,n},\varphi_{Q,n},\chi_{Q,n},D_{Q,n})$ at each finite layer $K_n$. It is obtained from the corresponding statement over the base layer `...baseSmoothPointStalks...` and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_of_eq_three_of_dvd), the packaging step in the analysis of the semistable reduction of modular curves at $q$.
